# Every function the `munsu` binary cannot reach, and why it is allowed to stay.
#
# `.github/scripts/deadcode.sh check` compares this file against
# `deadcode ./cmd/munsu` in both directions: unreachable in the tree but missing
# here is red, and listed here but reachable (or gone) is red too. So a new
# function that nothing in the binary can call cannot land quietly, and a line
# here cannot outlive the function it waives.
#
# This register contains only current, reviewed exceptions. Every reason states
# the premise, the test that pins it, and the condition that invalidates it.
# New unreachable functions must be wired, deleted, or added here with the same
# standard; the comparison never treats a reason as proof.
#
# Columns are tab-separated: file <TAB> function <TAB> reason
#
# No line numbers on purpose: they are not part of an entry's identity, and
# including them would rewrite this file on every unrelated edit above a
# function. Run `.github/scripts/deadcode.sh list` for the current keys.
#
# The set is the union across every GOOS in .github/build-tags.manifest, so a
# GOOS-gated file is covered even though only one build ever compiles it. That
# is why the linux and darwin halves of a `_linux.go`/`_darwin.go` pair both
# appear below, and why this file reads the same on a laptop and on the runner.

# --- Known open bugs, NOT accepted debt -------------------------------------
# A guard that exists, is complete, and cannot fire because nothing in the
# binary calls it. These are holes, not debt: the code was written to refuse
# something and the refusal can never happen. They are listed here only so the
# lane can go green; `deadcode.sh check` reprints every one as a warning on
# every single run, and each line names the issue that owns the verdict --
# wire it up or delete it. A line leaves this section with that issue, not
# before, and nobody may quietly demote one to accepted debt.
#
# `announce_open_bugs` runs on every `check`, so every line below is reprinted
# as a warning until its issue closes. An empty section is the intended resting
# state; it is empty right now.

# --- Current exceptions ------------------------------------------------------
# These are not an imported backlog. Each is a deliberate exception to the
# shipped binary's reachability graph and must be removed when its stated
# invalidation condition becomes true.
internal/fleet/process_args.go	splitProcessCommand	GOOS-union exception: process_inventory_darwin.go calls this parser on darwin, while linux and windows have no caller. Pinned by TestDarwinCommandSplitterPreservesQuotedHome in internal/fleet/writer_runtime_test.go; remove this exception if the darwin inventory path is deleted or the parser becomes reachable on every analyzed GOOS.
internal/fleet/process_args.go	writerKindForArgs	GOOS-union exception: process_inventory_linux.go and process_inventory_darwin.go call this classifier, while the windows build has no caller. Pinned by TestWriterKindForArgsParsesHomeFormsAndCanonicalAliases in internal/fleet/writer_runtime_test.go; remove this exception if the platform inventories converge or the windows inventory gains a caller.
internal/config/project_overlay.go	StoreProjectOverlay	Test-only writer retained in production config because project overlays are operator-authored documents: production reads them through fleet ResolveProjectSnapshot -> config.LoadProjectOverlay, but no shipped command writes them. Pinned by TestProjectOverlayDocumentCarriesBackend and the cross-package fleet fixture uses; move it to a test-owned seam or delete this exception when a production overlay-writing command is added.
internal/fleet/task_handoff_transaction.go	SetHandoffCrashHookForTest	Test-only crash-boundary seam retained in fleet because internal/cli/captain_handoff_test.go is a different package and must inject subprocess crash points without exposing the package-private hook. Pinned by TestTaskShowRecoversPendingTransferAndReadsCanonicalState; move it to a test-only external seam or delete this exception if the cross-package subprocess test no longer needs injection.
internal/home/wake_lease.go	ReclaimExpiredLeases	Test-only durable reclaim seam retained because home and orchestrator tests must create expired lease state and observe re-enqueue, resolved-event suppression, and lease-file removal before ClaimWakes runs. Pinned by TestPreparedResolutionDoesNotSuppressLeaseReclaim in internal/home/wake_resolve_test.go and TestDispatchWake_DeferredWakeReclaimsAfterLeaseExpiry in internal/orchestrator/wake_dispatch_test.go; delete this exception if those tests gain an equivalent public setup path or the reclaim operation becomes a shipped command.
internal/home/wake_lease.go	reclaimExpiredLeasesAt	Test-only injectable-clock reclaim seam: the production claim path reclaims through reclaimExpiredLeasesLocked (wake_lease.go, called from claimWakesLocked) under the already-held wake lock, while reclaimExpiredLeasesAt takes the lock itself and accepts a now func so tests can drive expiry deterministically. Pinned by the same expired-lease reclaim tests as ReclaimExpiredLeases, which it wraps; delete this exception if the wrapper is inlined into the shipped reclaim path or gains a binary caller.
internal/home/wake_lease.go	LeaseFilePath	Test-only lease-path helper: production lease locate/mutate now goes through validatedLeasePath (wake_mutation.go), which validates the id and refuses traversal, so LeaseFilePath is reached only by home and orchestrator tests that construct expected lease paths and plant lease state (for example internal/home/wake_mutation_test.go TestRecoverWakeMutation* and internal/home/wake_lease_test.go). Delete this exception if a shipped caller needs an unvalidated lease path or the tests adopt validatedLeasePath for their setup.
internal/fleet/busy_authority.go	BusyReading.Valid	Additive-slice exception: BusyReading is only constructed by ReadBusy, which has no binary consumer until ADR-0021 task A3 wires orchestrator DispatchWake through it. Pinned by TestBusyReading_StringAndValid in internal/fleet/busy_authority_test.go; delete this exception when A3 gives ReadBusy a binary caller or the authority is deleted.
internal/orchestrator/process_event_source.go	RegisterProcessEvent	Additive-slice exception: the durable process-event source is introduced additively by ADR-0021 task P1 with no binary consumer until P2 (merged-PR retirement instance) or C1 (condition-action) wires it into the supervision watcher. Pinned by TestProcessEvent_ResolutionSpendsExactlyOneWakeCarryingGeneration in internal/orchestrator/process_event_source_test.go; delete this exception when P2/C1 gives the source a binary caller or the source is deleted.
internal/orchestrator/process_event_source.go	EvaluateProcessEvent	Additive-slice exception: the durable process-event source is introduced additively by ADR-0021 task P1 with no binary consumer until P2 (merged-PR retirement instance) or C1 (condition-action) wires it into the supervision watcher. Pinned by TestProcessEvent_ResolutionSpendsExactlyOneWakeCarryingGeneration in internal/orchestrator/process_event_source_test.go; delete this exception when P2/C1 gives the source a binary caller or the source is deleted.
